WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.167
Week 26: Conditional, Courtesy, and Hypothesis. make a tactful request evaluate options state hypothetical consequences

2
00:00:09.167 --> 00:00:22.903
Form and meaning. Applying the form. The conditional uses the same irregular stems as the future (haría, tendría, podría) plus -ía endings, and softens requests and hypothetical statements.

3
00:00:22.903 --> 00:00:46.793
Model set. Yo haría lo mismo. Tendría más tiempo si trabajara menos. ¿Podrías ayudarme, por favor? Dijo que vendría mañana. Diría que sí, pero no estoy seguro. I would do the same. I would have more time if I worked less. Could you help me, please? He/she said they would come tomorrow. I would say yes, but I'm not sure.

4
00:00:46.793 --> 00:00:57.072
Contrastive practice. Change the person, time, number, or level of formality in each model. Preserve the communicative purpose while the grammar changes.

5
00:00:57.072 --> 00:01:10.359
Production check. Say one original sentence for each function: make a tactful request; evaluate options; state hypothetical consequences. Then write it and compare the spoken and written forms.

6
00:01:10.359 --> 00:01:35.017
Model language. Yo haría lo mismo. — I would do the same. Tendría más tiempo si trabajara menos. — I would have more time if I worked less. ¿Podrías ayudarme, por favor? — Could you help me, please? Dijo que vendría mañana. — He/she said they would come tomorrow. Diría que sí, pero no estoy seguro. — I would say yes, but I'm not sure.

7
00:01:35.017 --> 00:01:45.022
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
